d 'ARDLDML': module to perform DML-Bounds: ARDL bounds testing for cointegration with many persistent controls
d
d	 ardldml implements DML-Bounds, the procedure of Villena
d (2026): a test for a long-run (cointegrating) relationship
d between    depvar and focalvar when the conditioning set is
d high-dimensional and may itself carry stochastic trends.    The
d classical ARDL bounds test of Pesaran, Shin and Smith (2001)
d brackets one unknown: whether the tested regressors are I(0)	 
d or I(1). With a large, persistent control set a second unknown
d appears. Partialling out controls that carry stochastic trends   
d can absorb part of the long-run variation that identifies the
d error-correction relation. What then governs the null is not the 
d   integration order of the original regressors but the
d {bf:effective integrated count} k-tilde: the number of stochastic
d trends    that survive residualisation.  k-tilde = k puts the
d null at the classical I(1) endpoint, k-tilde = 0 at the I(0)
d endpoint, and    anything between lands inside the bracket.	
d The procedure has three stages. A balanced first stage projects
d the differenced outcome on stationary regressors only and the   
d lagged levels on the control levels, cross-fitted over contiguous
d time blocks separated by an h-observation buffer. The lagged	 
d levels are then residualised, and the F form of the Wald test of
d joint insignificance is computed on the orthogonalised terms.   
d Inference comes from a restricted system wild bootstrap that
d regenerates the outcome and the focal regressor jointly under the
d    null. 
d
d KW: ARDL
d KW: cointegration
d KW: bounds
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260825
d
d Author:   Merwan Roudane, NA
d Support: email  merwanroudane920@@gmail.com
d
f ardldml.ado
f ardldml.mata
f ardldml.sthlp
f ardldml_buildmlib.do
f ardldml_estat.ado
f ardldml_example.do
f ardldml_examples.sthlp
f ardldml_mcheck.do
f ardldml_methods.sthlp
f ardldml_p.ado
f ardldml_passthrough.dta
f ardldml_postestimation.sthlp
f ardldml_validate.do
f ../_/_ardldml_blockgraph.ado
f ../_/_ardldml_nullgraph.ado
f ../l/lardldml.mlib
